# Collision detector model of the simulated ARC Mate: EXACTLY the
# plant's values (arcmate.arm), for the residual floor. A real model comes
# from identification; model_perturbed.arm stands in for one.
observer 50 0.3 0.01
# motor torque per amp: 1.5 * pole pairs * psi (j1.conf .. j6.conf)
kt 1 1.1112
kt 2 1.1112
kt 3 1.1112
kt 4 0.36
kt 5 0.36
kt 6 0.36
# thresholds: J thr0 [Nm] thr_v [Nm s/rad] thr_s [Nm] vs [rad/s]
# (0: not checked); ~1.5 x the residual floor of model_perturbed.arm
# over tests/inc_motion_suite.txt: moving (thr0), and the stiction band
# near standstill (thr_s, gone by ~2 vs)
thresh 1 14 0 15 0.15
thresh 2 17 0 21 0.15
thresh 3 13 0 18 0.15
thresh 4 2.7 0 2.5 0.15
thresh 5 2.8 0 2 0.15
thresh 6 0.9 0 1.2 0.15
# plus 20 % of the dynamic torque |tau - g(q)|: inertia errors at full
# acceleration from standstill (LinuxCNC's trapezoidal moves and jogs)
threl 1 0.2
threl 2 0.2
threl 3 0.2
threl 4 0.2
threl 5 0.2
threl 6 0.2
# plus the rotors' acceleration torque: through the elastic gears the
# rotor runs ahead of the link at every jerk (LinuxCNC's trapezoids)
thrrot 1 1
thrrot 2 1
thrrot 3 1
thrrot 4 1
thrrot 5 1
thrrot 6 1
dh 1 0     0    0.45 0
dh 2 0.15 -90   0    -90
dh 3 0.60  0    0    0
dh 4 0.12 -90   0.65 0
dh 5 0     90   0    0
dh 6 0    -90   0.10 0
link 1 40  0     0     -0.10  1.2  1.2  0.8  0 0 0
link 2 25  0.30  0     0.05   0.20 1.00 1.00 0 0 0
link 3 15  0.05  0.10  0      0.40 0.40 0.15 0 0 0
link 4 6   0     0     0.15   0.06 0.06 0.02 0 0 0
link 5 3   0     0.03  0      0.01 0.01 0.01 0 0 0
link 6 1   0     0     0.04   0.002 0.002 0.002 0 0 0
motor 1 120 0.00035 0.02 8
motor 2 120 0.00035 0.02 8
motor 3 100 0.00035 0.02 8
motor 4 80  0.00003 0.01 1.5
motor 5 80  0.00003 0.01 1.5
motor 6 50  0.00003 0.01 1.5
fric 1 10 15 0.05 20
fric 2 12 18 0.05 25
fric 3 8  12 0.05 15
fric 4 1  1.5 0.05 1
fric 5 1  1.5 0.05 1
fric 6 0.5 0.8 0.05 0.5
